  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added an explicit embedded-REPL input-failure exit policy, kept the standalone non-TTY default fatal, disabled only doctest user-exception exit mutation, and made random-seed setup output fail closed. End-to-end regressions prove expected traceback exit 0, mismatch exit 1, malformed worker exit 1, and existing piped CLI failure behavior. Linux x64 exact-current focused, CLI, architecture, strict, and portable (443/443) receipts pass at 5c64fba; the full changed-file build/unit/compiler/integration selection passed at the byte-identical pre-rebase source 3b381e3. Physical Apple M1 Max macOS 26.4 at exact byte-identical source 3b381e3 passed focused, CLI smoke, and docs verification (127 passed, 2 xfailed, 4 skipped, 0 failed). Linux arm64 and Windows are not applicable because the change has no architecture or OS branch; the required macOS run covers the original host failure.",
    "risks": [
      "The opt-out is intentionally available only to explicit REPL embedders; callers that disable it must retain their own output/error acceptance boundary."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Retain these exit semantics through the remaining shared integrations and the final exact frozen-source first-party release workflow."
    ]
  }
